---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release, url } from '../lib/publication';
const claim = (id: string) => release.claims.find(c => c.id === id);
const source = (id: string) => {
  const item = claim(id);
  return item ? url(`/sources/${item.evidenceIds[0]}/`) : url('/sources/');
};
const rain = claim('C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-india-20260923');
const premises = claim('C-NSO-PREMISES-2018');
const sufficiency = claim('C-NSO-SUFFICIENCY-2018');
const functionSurvey = claim('C-JJM-FUNCTIONALITY-2024');
const karnataka = claim('C-KA-DROUGHT-ORDER-20260922');
const foodBudget = claim('C-NSO-HCES-FOODSHARE-202324');
---
<Site title="The cost is not in the rain gauge" description="An evidence-led account of potential effects on livelihoods and unequal water access, with dated surveys and no invented 2026 loss total.">
  <PageHeader title="The cost is not in the rain gauge" eyebrow="People / livelihoods / unequal access" description="Rainfall describes weather. The human story needs records of crops, work, prices, service and the time people spend finding water." />
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">01</span><div><p class="eyebrow">The line we cannot yet cross</p><h2>A deficit is not a loss estimate.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="grid-2"><p class="g11-pull"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · IMD reported</span><br />India's rainfall was <strong>−14.9%</strong> against the normal for 1 June–23 September 2026. <a href={rain ? source(rain.id) : url('/sources/')}>Source and dates ↗</a></p><div class="g11-clock"><p>That graphic cannot count failed harvests, lost wages, tanker spending, illness or migration. We have no approved 2026 series that establishes those outcomes or a national total. It would be wrong to multiply one rainfall percentage into an economic loss.</p></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">02</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Different starting points</p><h2>Access was uneven before this season.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="g11-signal-grid">{premises && <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · 2018 survey</span><span>Rural households</span><strong>58.2%</strong><p>reported a drinking-water facility within their premises. This is not a 2026 tap-service measure.</p><a href={source(premises.id)}>NSO survey ↗</a></article>}{premises && <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · 2018 survey</span><span>Urban households</span><strong>80.7%</strong><p>reported a facility within their premises under the same survey definition.</p><a href={source(premises.id)}>NSO survey ↗</a></article>}{functionSurvey && <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · 2024 sample</span><span>Already-covered villages</span><strong>86.5%</strong><p>of surveyed households with taps had received water in the preceding seven days. This sample is not all rural India.</p><a href={source(functionSurvey.id)}>Functionality assessment ↗</a></article>}</div>
    {sufficiency && <p class="small muted">In the same 2018 NSO survey, 87.6% of rural and 90.9% of urban households said their principal source supplied sufficient water throughout the year. That is self-reported sufficiency, not a 2026 quality test or daily service log. <a href={source(sufficiency.id)}>Survey record ↗</a></p>}
    <p class="g11-pull">Those are three distinct measurements, not one improving or worsening time series.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">03</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Where harm would appear</p><h2>Follow the consequence, then ask for the record.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="grid-3"><article class="g11-branch"><p class="eyebrow">Farms and food</p><h3>From rain to harvest is not a straight line.</h3><p>Which crop, at which stage, on irrigated or rainfed land? A claim of damage needs dated sowing, yield or crop-survey evidence in that place, plus other possible causes. <a href={karnataka ? source(karnataka.id) : url('/sources/')}>Karnataka's order</a> directs a survey; its result is not approved here.</p><a href={url('/response/')}>See the declaration stage ↗</a></article><article class="g11-branch"><p class="eyebrow">Work and prices</p><h3>Trace a disruption before pricing it.</h3><p>Check a named supply system, production interruption and matched wholesale or retail series. Simultaneous rain and price changes do not establish that one caused the other. No 2026 loss or inflation attribution is published here.</p><a href={url('/journalists/')}>Records to request ↗</a></article><article class="g11-branch"><p class="eyebrow">Households</p><h3>A pipe, a schedule, a safe sample.</h3><p>A <a href="https://documents1.worldbank.org/curated/en/422671468269113902/pdf/721050WP0Box370tinuous0Water0Supply.pdf">December 2009 Water and Sanitation Program guidance note</a> describes tanks, pumps, treatment devices and purchased water as coping responses to intermittent urban supply. It is historical mechanism, not evidence of 2026 coping or costs. Which households could afford a buffer, and whether a shared source constrained them, needs local records.</p><a href={url('/water-and-people/')}>Understand access ↗</a></article></div>
    {foodBudget && <div class="g11-clock"><span class="g11-tag history">Historical budget context · NSO 2023–24</span><h3>Why food prices would matter to household budgets</h3><p>Food made up <strong>47.04%</strong> of average rural and <strong>39.68%</strong> of average urban monthly per-person expenditure in NSO's 2023–24 survey, excluding imputation of selected free government-provided items. These are national rural/urban averages, not the shares for low-income households. They do not establish a 2026 food-price rise or any water-linked household loss. <a href={source(foodBudget.id)}>Survey factsheet and denominator ↗</a></p></div>}
  </div></section>
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">04</span><div><p class="eyebrow">What would change this page</p><h2>Show impact, and show recovery.</h2></div></div><p>For each named place, match weather and source records to delivered service, crop results, prices and household experience on the same dates. Publish the denominator, who was observed, what changed and alternative explanations. Track restoration too: a repaired scheme or replenished source matters only when its outcome is measured.</p><div class="g11-epilogue"><p class="eyebrow">The current verdict</p><h3>Exposure is plausible. Realized 2026 losses are not verified here.</h3><p>That gap is a reporting assignment, not reassurance that no one has been harmed.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={url('/states/')}>Start with a place ↗</a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/data-status/')}>See missing evidence ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
</Site>
